    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0526" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.113/10547a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Collector of Customs at Douglas,
                        Arizona</hi><anchor n="67" xml:id="d492-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-01">May 1, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mexican Embassy at Washington has advised this Department that Agua Prieta
                    surrendered to Federals this morning, that rebel troops are without necessary
                    food supplies, and requested that no further restrictions be placed on
                    exportation of food and other supplies. You are accordingly authorized to permit
                    unrestricted exportation of all food and other supplies not specifically covered
                    by embargo proclamation of January 7, 1924.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d492-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry L. Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d492-f1" n="67" type="source" xml:id="d492-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Collector of
                    Customs at Nogales, Arizona, mentioning Nogales, Mexico, as the place which
                    surrendered.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d492-f2" n="68" xml:id="d492-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="frus1924v02#pg_428"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1924, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 428</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
